Exact blocking condition:
At the end of _serialized_repository_recovery, after successful root Git
materialization and immutable release staging, _lock_worktree_write_barrier
observes the fixture's repos/app/created directory:
  uid=0, gid=1001, mode=2770, durable barrier record absent.
The directory inherited the retained default POSIX ACL from the repository.
Its group-write bit violates the required sealed new-object state. The
tracked-path second pass raises S12_1_RECOVERY_WORKTREE_BARRIER_RED.
The exception handler then invokes canonical rollback; its admission encounters
the same unjournaled, group-writable object and fails with the same safe code.
Therefore neither successful deployment nor its required rollback path has
been proved jointly satisfiable. The earlier in-body failure test did not
exercise this post-materialization boundary.

