Smallest additional design/authorization needed:
A reviewed prospective ACL-safe materialization/successor contract for new and
replaced target objects, including default-ACL propagation. It must prove
writer exclusion while objects are created, bind object identity/creator and
target metadata before any release, journal finite transitions durably, and
make interrupted checkout + rollback verifiable. Preserve the R12 finite
historical-gap contract and legacy evidence unchanged. Do not infer creator
or provenance from content equality, root ownership or current mode alone.

Not acceptable: after-the-fact chmod/chown, accepting group-writable unbound
objects, deleting old markers, adding a new unreviewed R12 path list at runtime,
or changing tests to hide the inherited ACL. No such action was taken.

